    <other_details id="References">Archetypes: openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-ORGANISATION.generic_organisation.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.part_of.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.party_membership.v1, openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-PARTY_RELATIONSHIP.role_assignment.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.address.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.electronic_communication.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.person.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.structured_name.v1. Structure derived from the openEHR CKM demographic drafts openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-ORGANISATION.organisation.v0 and PARTY_IDENTITY.organisation_name.v0, after ISO/DTS 27527:2007 Provider Identification. Addresses, telecom and contact persons use the published CKM clusters openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.address.v1, electronic_communication.v1 and person.v1. Aligned with the HL7 FHIR R4 (4.0.1) resource Organization (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/).</other_details>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>An organisation: its names by kind, identifiers, types, whether it is active, a description, contact persons, postal and electronic contacts, and the organisation it is part of, the groups and organisations it is a member of and the roles it holds.</purpose>
      <keywords>organisation</keywords>
      <keywords>healthcare provider</keywords>
      <keywords>hospital</keywords>
      <keywords>department</keywords>
      <keywords>practice</keywords>
      <use>Use for a hospital, a practice, a department, a ward, a laboratory, an insurer or another organisation with a legal or administrative standing. A part names the organisation it is part of through a part of relationship of its own; a care provider, a group or an agent records its membership of the organisation in its own party, and a patient a care relationship to it.</use>
      <misuse>Not for a care team, a household or another group without a legal or administrative standing: use GROUP-CareTeam.v1 or GROUP-generic.v1.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openehr-reference-content contributors</copyright>
    </details>
  </description>
